      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving it.Let me check the `Traffic2` enum to understand the `getLabel` method.Now I have a clear picture of the code. Let me write the improved test with better understandability — removing unused imports and the dead helper, naming the function variable clearly, and grouping assertions by scenario.Now let me run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version improves understandability by: removing all unused imports and the dead `assertLongArrayEquals` helper, promoting the label function to a named constant `GET_LABEL`, and grouping the 11 assertions into four clearly commented blocks (label match, no match → default, null input → default, null default → null)."
